",{"children":"This mirrors the transformation occurring at MIT and Stanford, but with a distinctly Chinese scale: SJTU aims to produce 100 breakthrough research outputs annually through AI-accelerated scientific discovery."}]]}],["$","hr","50",{"style":{"border":"none","borderTop":"1px solid #1a1a1a","margin":"32px 0"}}],["$","h2","52",{"style":{"fontSize":"28px","fontWeight":"600","margin":"40px 0 20px","color":"#f5f5f5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"National Standards for Humanoid Robots: From Prototype to Industry"}]]}],["$","p","54",{"style":{"fontSize":"16px","lineHeight":"1.8","margin":"16px 0","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"While education reforms capture headlines, China's approval of the first national standards for humanoid robots represents perhaps more consequential industrial policy. These standards establish the technical specifications, safety protocols, and interoperability requirements necessary for mass production."}]]}],["$","h3","56",{"style":{"fontSize":"22px","fontWeight":"600","margin":"32px 0 16px","color":"#f5f5f5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"Standard Framework Overview"}]]}],["$","div","65",{"style":{"overflowX":"auto","margin":"24px 0"},"children":["$","table",null,{"style":{"width":"100%","borderCollapse":"collapse","fontSize":"14px"},"children":[["$","thead",null,{"children":["$","tr",null,{"children":[["$","th","0",{"style":{"borderBottom":"2px solid #22d3ee","padding":"12px 16px","textAlign":"left","fontWeight":"600","color":"#22d3ee"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"Category"}]]}],["$","th","1",{"style":{"borderBottom":"2px solid #22d3ee","padding":"12px 16px","textAlign":"left","fontWeight":"600","color":"#22d3ee"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"Standard Scope"}]]}],["$","th","2",{"style":{"borderBottom":"2px solid #22d3ee","padding":"12px 16px","textAlign":"left","fontWeight":"600","color":"#22d3ee"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"Implementation Tim